From: whatshu <shussm@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: quiesce old session interrupts during role changes

Ending the B-session before forcing host mode raises session-end and
reset interrupts on the ESP32-S31. These can continuously retrigger in
the old device role, starving the thread that must force the new mode.
Mask those old-role events before ending the session; host initialization
installs its interrupt mask after the mode change.

A software role switch without HNP or SRP does not need the OTG negotiation
interrupt in host mode. Leave it masked when initializing common interrupts
so the pending session-end event cannot starve HCD startup either. Keep
existing behavior for controllers using hardware OTG session management.

Signed-off-by: whatshu <shussm@qq.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
@@ -145,6 +145,14 @@
 		dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(hsotg, 0);
 
 	if (role == USB_ROLE_HOST) {
+		if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
+			u32 mask = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GINTMSK);
+
+			/* The old B-session ends before host mode is forced. */
+			mask &= ~(GINTSTS_OTGINT | GINTSTS_USBRST |
+				  GINTSTS_RESETDET);
+			dwc2_writel(hsotg, mask, GINTMSK);
+		}
 		already = dwc2_ovr_avalid(hsotg, true);
 	} else if (role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE) {
 		already = dwc2_ovr_bvalid(hsotg, true);
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
@@ -50,7 +50,10 @@
 	dwc2_writel(hsotg, 0xffffffff, GINTSTS);
 
 	/* Enable the interrupts in the GINTMSK */
-	intmsk = GINTSTS_MODEMIS | GINTSTS_OTGINT;
+	intmsk = GINTSTS_MODEMIS;
+	if (!hsotg->role_sw || hsotg->params.otg_caps.hnp_support ||
+	    hsotg->params.otg_caps.srp_support)
+		intmsk |= GINTSTS_OTGINT;
 
 	if (!hsotg->params.host_dma)
 		intmsk |= GINTSTS_RXFLVL;
